tip: | Look at the courier. | The parcel hides the middle of the figure, so it is drawn as part of the same pose: arms under it, weight leaning back a little.
tip: 1 | Pose with the load. | Merge the figure and the parcel into one shape. If the two look stuck together rather than carried, move the arms, not the box.
tip: 4 | A box still has three faces. | The parcel is the crate again, small: light top, mid left, dark right, and a label to say which way up it goes.
tip: | Mirrors flip everything. | The label and the cap peak swap sides, and the light does too. A flip is fine for most things, but look at text and at anything held in one hand.
